<section class="hero" id="home">
 <div class="hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
 <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> THERMAL ENGINEERING. WITHOUT LIMITS.</p><h1>Power ahead.<br>Keep your <em>cool.</em></h1><p class="hero-description">When performance creates heat, we create possibilities. Custom thermal solutions, engineered and manufactured for your next breakthrough.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="btn" href="#solutions">Explore our solutions <span>↗</span></a><button class="text-btn" data-inquiry>Talk to an engineer <span>↗</span></button></div><div class="hero-proof"><span class="seal">✓</span><span>ISO 9001:2015 certified</span><i></i><span>Made in Ontario. Built for your world.</span></div></div>
 <div class="hero-product"><div class="orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="orbit orbit-two"></div><span class="technical-label label-top">01 / ENGINEERED TO PERFORM</span><img id="hero-product-image" src="assets/hero-heatsink.webp" alt="ITS aluminum heat sink with embedded copper heat pipes" fetchpriority="high"><div class="product-tag"><span class="status-dot"></span><span id="hero-product-label">Embedded heat pipe technology</span><button id="hero-switch" aria-label="Show liquid cooling product">↻</button></div><span class="technical-label label-bottom">PRECISION IN EVERY DETAIL <span>+</span></span></div>
 <div class="hero-bottom"><a href="#solutions">SCROLL TO DISCOVER <span>↓</span></a><span>DESIGNED. SIMULATED. MANUFACTURED. TESTED.</span><span>43.51° N / 80.21° W</span></div>
</section>
<section class="trust-strip" aria-label="Company capabilities"><span>From the first concept<br><strong>to the final component.</strong></span><div><b>75+</b><span>years of combined<br>engineering experience</span></div><div><b>5-axis</b><span>precision CNC<br>manufacturing</span></div><div><b>In-house</b><span>friction stir<br>welding technology</span></div><div><b>North America</b><span>engineering & manufacturing<br>with global production partners</span></div></section>
<section class="section solutions" id="solutions">
 <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE RIGHT SOLUTION</p><h2>Every thermal challenge.<br><span>A better way to cool.</span></h2></div><p>Air. Liquid. Or a custom combination.<br>Explore the technologies that move heat<br>out of the way of progress.</p></div>
 <div class="solution-toolbar"><div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Product family"><button role="tab" id="tab-all" aria-controls="product-grid" aria-selected="true" data-filter="all">All solutions <span>08</span></button><button role="tab" id="tab-air" aria-controls="product-grid" aria-selected="false" data-filter="air">Air cooled</button><button role="tab" id="tab-liquid" aria-controls="product-grid" aria-selected="false" data-filter="liquid">Liquid cooled</button></div><label class="search"><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span><input id="product-search" type="search" placeholder="Find a solution" aria-label="Search thermal solutions"></label></div>
 <div id="product-grid" class="product-grid" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-all"></div><p id="no-results" hidden>No solutions match your search. Try “copper”, “air”, or “cold plate”.</p>
 <div class="solution-help"><span>Not sure where to start? <strong>Tell us what’s getting too hot.</strong></span><button class="line-link" data-finder>Find your cooling approach <span>↗</span></button></div>
</section>
<section class="industry-section" id="industries"><div class="section section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / BUILT FOR YOUR INDUSTRY</p><h2>Behind the systems<br>that move us forward.</h2></div><p>From power conversion to electrification,<br>thermal performance makes the difference.</p></div><div class="industry-explorer"><div class="industry-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Industries"><button role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="industry-panel" id="market-power" data-market="power"><span>01</span>Power & automation <b>↗</b></button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="industry-panel" id="market-energy" data-market="energy"><span>02</span>Clean energy <b>↗</b></button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="industry-panel" id="market-satellite" data-market="satellite"><span>03</span>Satellite & telecom <b>↗</b></button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="industry-panel" id="market-aerospace" data-market="aerospace"><span>04</span>Aerospace & defense <b>↗</b></button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="industry-panel" id="market-ev" data-market="ev"><span>05</span>EV & battery <b>↗</b></button></div><div class="industry-visual" id="industry-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="market-power"><img id="market-image" src="assets/power.webp" alt="Power conversion and industrial automation applications" loading="lazy"><div class="industry-caption"><span class="eyebrow" id="market-label">POWER & AUTOMATION</span><h3 id="market-title">More power.<br>Less thermal compromise.</h3><p id="market-description">Custom heat sinks and cold plates for power converters, motor drives, UPS systems and industrial automation.</p><button class="line-link" id="market-inquiry">Discuss your application <span>↗</span></button></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section process-section" id="engineering"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / ONE ENGINEERING PARTNER</p><h2>From “what if”<br><span>to working hardware.</span></h2></div><p>Thermal and mechanical design, simulation,<br>manufacturing and testing. Connected<br>from the very first conversation.</p></div><div class="process-layout"><div class="process-image"><img id="process-image" src="assets/temperature-model.webp" alt="Thermal simulation of a liquid cold plate" loading="lazy"><div class="process-image-caption"><span id="process-caption">SIMULATE. ITERATE. OPTIMIZE.</span><span id="process-counter">01 — 04</span></div></div><div class="process-steps"><button class="process-step active" aria-expanded="true" data-step="0"><span class="step-number">01</span><div><h3>Define & discover</h3><p>Start with your heat load, temperature targets, available space and production goals. We turn the constraints into a clear design brief.</p></div><span class="step-icon">−</span></button><button class="process-step" aria-expanded="false" data-step="1"><span class="step-number">02</span><div><h3>Design & simulate</h3><p>CFD, parametric studies and iterative optimization explore the thermal design. SolidWorks supports mechanical design and integration.</p></div><span class="step-icon">+</span></button><button class="process-step" aria-expanded="false" data-step="2"><span class="step-number">03</span><div><h3>Machine & manufacture</h3><p>Five-axis CNC machining and friction stir welding bring the design to life at our Ontario facility, with trusted partners for high-volume production.</p></div><span class="step-icon">+</span></button><button class="process-step" aria-expanded="false" data-step="3"><span class="step-number">04</span><div><h3>Test & deliver</h3><p>Experiments and prototype evaluation check thermal performance against your project requirements before moving toward production.</p></div><span class="step-icon">+</span></button></div></div></section>
<section class="fsw-section"><div class="fsw-photo"><img src="assets/fsw-process.webp" alt="Friction stir welding tool machining a metal workpiece" loading="lazy"><span class="eyebrow">IN-HOUSE / GUELPH, ONTARIO</span></div><div class="fsw-copy"><p class="eyebrow">THE CONNECTION MAKES THE DIFFERENCE</p><h2>A stronger bond.<br>A cooler future.</h2><p>Friction stir welding joins metal without melting it. For liquid cold plates, that means a precise way to seal complex internal channels while limiting distortion.</p><div class="fsw-benefits"><span>↗ Joint integrity</span><span>↗ Leak-tight construction</span><span>↗ Dimensional stability</span><span>↗ Process repeatability</span></div><button class="btn btn-light" id="fsw-learn">Explore the technology <span>↗</span></button></div></section>
<section class="section results-section" id="results"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / ENGINEERING IN ACTION</p><h2>Real challenges.<br><span>Measurable progress.</span></h2></div><p>A closer look at the thinking<br>behind our thermal solutions.</p></div><div class="case-feature"><div class="case-copy"><p class="eyebrow">CASE STUDY / RF & TELECOMMUNICATIONS</p><h3>Turning down the heat<br>on RF performance.</h3><div class="case-stat"><b>20<span>°C</span></b><p>up to 20°C reduction<br>in peak temperature</p></div><p>ITS’s embedded heat pipe design improved heat distribution in a wireless solid-state amplifier. Explore the thermal models to see the difference.</p><span class="small-note">Reported project result from the ITS company presentation. Results depend on application and operating conditions.</span></div><div class="comparison"><div class="thermal-images"><div class="thermal-base"><img src="assets/thermal-after.webp" alt="Thermal model after the ITS heat pipe redesign" loading="lazy"></div><div class="thermal-overlay" id="thermal-overlay"><img src="assets/thermal-before.webp" alt="Thermal model of the original amplifier cooling design" loading="lazy"></div><span class="comparison-label before">ORIGINAL DESIGN</span><span class="comparison-label after">ITS SOLUTION</span><div class="comparison-handle" id="comparison-handle">↔</div></div><label for="thermal-range">Drag to compare the thermal models <span>← →</span></label><input type="range" id="thermal-range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Compare original design with ITS solution"></div></div><div class="case-secondary"><img src="assets/bus-plate.webp" alt="Large-format ITS electric bus aluminum battery cold plate" loading="lazy"><div><p class="eyebrow">EV & BATTERY</p><h3>Big ambitions.<br>Larger-format cooling.</h3><p>An aluminum cold plate developed for electric bus battery cooling, measuring 1,450 × 610 × 15 mm (57 × 24 × 0.6 in).</p><button class="line-link" data-product="bus">Explore the project <span>↗</span></button></div><div class="dimension"><b>1,450<span>mm</span></b><span>ENGINEERED AT SCALE</span></div></div></section>
<section class="about-section" id="about"><div class="about-photo"><img src="assets/workshop.webp" alt="Inside the ITS Cooling manufacturing workshop in Ontario" loading="lazy"><span>OUR FACILITY / GUELPH, ONTARIO</span></div><div class="section about-copy"><p class="eyebrow">05 / PEOPLE. PRECISION. PARTNERSHIP.</p><h2>Small enough to listen.<br>Equipped to deliver.</h2><p>Founded in 2020, Innovative Thermal Solutions brings engineering and manufacturing together under one roof. We work alongside your team to solve cooling challenges, from a single prototype to production.</p><div class="about-facts"><div><b>6,000</b><span>sq ft facility</span></div><div><b>27</b><span>team members</span></div><div><b>2020</b><span>year founded</span></div></div><p class="small-note">Facility and team figures from the 2026 company presentation.</p><div class="quality-row"><span class="seal">✓</span><div><strong>Quality built into the process.</strong><p>ISO 9001:2015 certified. AS9100 and CGP / ITAR certification initiatives are in progress, as described in the company presentation.</p></div></div><button class="line-link" id="meet-team">Meet the people behind ITS <span>↗</span></button></div></section>
<section class="section faq-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">A FEW GOOD QUESTIONS</p><h2>Let’s clear<br><span>the air.</span></h2><button class="line-link" data-inquiry>Ask our engineers <span>↗</span></button></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Air cooling or liquid cooling: where do I start?<span>+</span></summary><p>Start with heat load, maximum component temperature, ambient conditions and space. Available airflow and coolant infrastructure also matter. ITS can evaluate these together and recommend an approach for your application.</p></details><details><summary>Can you work with our existing design?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. The ITS team collaborates with customers on product development, simulation and manufacturing. Share your current design, constraints and performance targets to begin the discussion.</p></details><details><summary>Do you manufacture in North America?<span>+</span></summary><p>ITS engineers and manufactures in Guelph, Ontario, with in-house CNC machining and friction stir welding. Trusted manufacturing partners in Asia support high-volume and cost-sensitive production requirements.</p></details><details><summary>What should I include in a project inquiry?<span>+</span></summary><p>Include your application, heat load, temperature limits, mounting envelope, quantities and timing. For liquid cooling, add coolant type, inlet temperature, flow rate and pressure-drop limits if available.</p></details><details><summary>How long will my project take?<span>+</span></summary><p>Timing depends on design complexity, materials, tooling, machining, fittings and validation requirements. Contact ITS with your scope and target date for a project-specific schedule.</p></details></div></section>
<section class="contact-section" id="contact"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> YOUR NEXT BREAKTHROUGH STARTS HERE</p><h2>Tell us what’s<br>getting <em>too hot.</em></h2><p>Bring us the challenge. Let’s engineer the solution.</p><button class="btn btn-dark" data-inquiry>Start your project <span>↗</span></button></div><div class="contact-details"><span>ENGINEERING & SALES</span><a href="mailto:Engineering@itscooling.com">Engineering@itscooling.com ↗</a><a href="tel:+15197634454">+1 (519) 763-4454 ↗</a><p>290 Southgate Drive, Unit #2<br>Guelph, ON N1G 4P5, Canada</p><span>MON–FRI / 8:30 AM–5:00 PM EASTERN</span></div></section>
</main>
